{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ships as a separate library target alongside "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It provides a single domain plugin ("},{"code":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), a state slice, an action enum, and a pluggable challenge generator. For task-oriented integration, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For the underlying plugin contract, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Library-target","type":"heading","text":"Library target"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product as a target dependency, then import it where you wire the store and present the gate sheet:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxParentalGate"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The package vends three library products: "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Pull in only what you use."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Types","type":"heading","text":"Types"},{"level":3,"anchor":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"heading","text":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-bound domain plugin generic over the host app’s root state and action types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@MainActor","public struct ParentalGatePlugin<RootState, RootAction>: SwiduxPlugin {","    public typealias State = RootState","    public typealias Action = RootAction","","    public init(","        state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, ParentalGateState>,","        action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (ParentalGateAction) -> RootAction,","        extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> ParentalGateAction?,","        challengeSource: ParentalChallengeSource = .standard","    )","","    public func reduce(state: inout RootState, action: RootAction) -> Effect<RootAction>?","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The three wiring closures follow the standard domain-plugin shape described in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a keypath into the host’s state, a lifter from local to root action, and an extractor from root to local action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"ParentalGateState","type":"heading","text":"ParentalGateState"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The state slice the plugin owns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public struct ParentalGateState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var pendingReason: String?","    public var challenge: MathChallenge?","    public var attempts: Int","    public var passedReasons: Set<String>","","    public init(","        pendingReason: String? = nil,","        challenge: MathChallenge? = nil,","        attempts: Int = 0,","        passedReasons: Set<String> = []","    )","}"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — non-","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" while a challenge is active. Drives sheet presentation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the currently-presented arithmetic problem.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — count of incorrect submissions against the current challenge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — reasons already cleared this session (see action semantics below).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"ParentalGateAction","type":"heading","text":"ParentalGateAction"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum ParentalGateAction: Sendable {","    case request(reason: String)","    case dismiss","    case regenerateChallenge","    case submitAnswer(Int)","    case answerAccepted(reason: String)","    case answerRejected","}"]},{"level":3,"anchor":"MathChallenge","type":"heading","text":"MathChallenge"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public struct MathChallenge: Sendable, Equatable {","    public let left: Int","    public let right: Int","    public let op: Op","","    public init(left: Int, right: Int, op: Op)","","    public var expected: Int","","    public enum Op: String, Sendable, CaseIterable {","        case plus, minus, times","","        public var symbol: String  \/\/ \"+\", \"−\", \"×\"","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"expected","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" computes the correct answer from "},{"code":"left","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"right","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"op","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"Op.symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns a display-friendly Unicode glyph (minus sign U+2212, multiplication sign U+00D7)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"ParentalChallengeSource","type":"heading","text":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A value-type holder for a challenge generator closure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public struct ParentalChallengeSource: Sendable {","    public var generate: @Sendable () -> MathChallenge","","    public init(generate: @escaping @Sendable () -> MathChallenge)","","    public static let standard: ParentalChallengeSource","    public static func fixed(_ challenge: MathChallenge) -> ParentalChallengeSource","}"]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource.standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — random, age-appropriate challenges. Plus and minus use operands in the 10–40 range; times uses 3–9. Subtraction is always non-negative."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource.fixed(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — always returns the supplied challenge. Use this in tests."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Action-semantics","type":"heading","text":"Action semantics","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGateAction"},{"type":"text","text":" case mutates the state slice as follows:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".request(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — If "},{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already contains "},{"code":"reason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the plugin returns an effect that immediately dispatches "},{"code":".answerAccepted(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and leaves "},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" unchanged. Otherwise, it sets "},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", generates a fresh "},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and resets "},{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".dismiss","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Clears "},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Does not modify "},{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".regenerateChallenge","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Replaces "},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a freshly generated one. Useful for a “new question” button."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".submitAnswer(Int)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Compares against "},{"code":"challenge.expected","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Returns an effect that dispatches either "},{"code":".answerAccepted(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (with the current "},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"code":".answerRejected","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". No-op if "},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".answerAccepted(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Inserts ","type":"text"},{"code":"reason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into ","type":"text"},{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".answerRejected","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Increments ","type":"text"},{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and regenerates ","type":"text"},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so the user faces a new problem.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Session-pass-behavior","type":"heading","text":"Session-pass behavior","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once a reason is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"passedReasons"},{"type":"text","text":", subsequent "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls for that same reason short-circuit: the plugin dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerAccepted(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" immediately without presenting a challenge. This is intentional — it lets feature reducers re-issue the gate request after re-entering a flow, while only prompting the user once per session."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"passedReasons"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set<String>"},{"type":"text","text":", so use distinct reason keys per gated action when you want them to clear independently. To force a re-challenge, mutate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.parentalGate.passedReasons"},{"type":"text","text":" from your own reducer (for example, in response to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app\/lock"},{"type":"text","text":" action)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Customizing-the-challenge","type":"heading","text":"Customizing the challenge","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"type":"text","text":" is a single-closure container. To plug in your own generator — different operand ranges, alternative operations, locale-specific phrasing of operands — construct one directly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let source = ParentalChallengeSource {","    let left = Int.random(in: 50...99)","    let right = Int.random(in: 50...99)","    return MathChallenge(left: left, right: right, op: .plus)","}","","let plugin = ParentalGatePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.parentalGate,","    action: AppAction.parentalGate,","    extractAction: { if case .parentalGate(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    challengeSource: source",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generator runs synchronously each time the plugin needs a new challenge (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".regenerateChallenge"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerRejected"},{"type":"text","text":"). Keep it cheap and pure — no I\/O."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","title":"Add a Parental Gate","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","title":"UndoPlugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"KeyValueStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","title":"Macros","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the two macros that generate the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Swidux"}}}